    'Single-variable differential calculus and the start of integral calculus, at the 4-credit intensity of a US engineering school. Limits, continuity, the derivative as a limit, rules including chain and implicit, related rates, extreme values, the Mean Value Theorem, curve sketching, optimization, antiderivatives, and the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus with area and accumulation. This is not a survey. You will compute by hand until the algebra is no longer the bottleneck, then interpret the number in a sentence.',
