    'An algebra-based conceptual physics course with required laboratory writeups, designed as the lab-science substitute for a working adult: OpenStax College Physics 2e plus PhET interactive simulations, not a university wet lab. You will measure, graph, estimate uncertainty, and write methods/results/limitations as if a skeptic had to reproduce the work. You will not pipette, ignite, or sit a 4-hour campus lab section. The syllabus is honest about that trade: conceptual + sims + one at-home measurement (phone stopwatch / meter) in place of a two-semester studio sequence. If a graduate school later demands a wet-lab physics sequence, this course will not be that, and you should say so.',
